    <string name="section_about">About the calculation</string>
    <string name="about_body">True solar time follows the actual position of the sun: first correct for the longitude offset from 120°E (4 minutes per degree), then add the equation of time caused by Earth orbital eccentricity and obliquity. The twelve shichen follow true solar time, starting with Zi at 23:00, two hours each.</string>

